:"பாராட்டு","gloss":"praising"}],"gloss":"praising"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"எல்லிடைப்","parts":[{"text":"எல்லிடைப்","lemma":"எல்லிடைப்","gloss":"in the night"}],"gloss":"in the night","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"படர்தந்தோனே","parts":[{"text":"படர்தந்தோனே","lemma":"படர்தந்தோனே","gloss":"he who came marching"}],"gloss":"he who came marching","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"கல்லென","parts":[{"text":"கல்","lemma":"கல்","gloss":"sound of bustle"},{"text":"என","lemma":"என","gloss":"making"}],"gloss":"with a bustling sound"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"வேந்தூர்","parts":[{"text":"வேந்து","lemma":"வேந்தன்","gloss":"king"},{"text":"ஊர்","lemma":"ஊர்","gloss":"riding"}],"gloss":"ridden by the king"},{"surface":"யானைக்கு","parts":[{"text":"யானை","lemma":"யானை","gloss":"elephant"},{"text":"க்கு","lemma":"க்கு","gloss":"dative suffix"}],"gloss":"for the elephant"},{"surface":"அல்லது","parts":[{"text":"அல்லது","lemma":"அல்","gloss":"except"}],"gloss":"except"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"ஏந்துவன்","parts":[{"text":"ஏந்துவன்","lemma":"ஏந்து","gloss":"he will raise"}],"gloss":"he will raise"},{"surface":"போலான்","parts":[{"text":"போலான்","lemma":"போல்","gloss":"he does not seem"}],"gloss":"he does not seem"},{"surface":"தன்","parts":[{"text":"தன்","lemma":"தன்","gloss":"his"}],"gloss":"his"},{"surface":"இலங்கிலை","parts":[{"text":"இலங்கு","lemma":"இலங்கு","gloss":"shining"},{"text":"இலை","lemma":"இலை","gloss":"leaf-blade"}],"gloss":"shining leaf-bladed"},{"surface":"வேலே","parts":[{"text":"வேல்","lemma":"வேல்","gloss":"spear"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"spear"}]}],"literal":"O many noble warriors! O many noble warriors! / Resembling the hair of young women, / placed for battle, the dense thorny fence / of the bustling military camp, O many noble warriors! / Protect your king too, with his drum-roaring army! / Guard your male elephant too, with its shining prominent tusks! / However many days your battle will last, for that many days, / where is the striking of those who strike? Those who struck, / he will not even go against them to strike. Therefore, / who are those who know the purpose he intended? / Avoid despising him thinking of your strength! Look there! / Like measuring the ground, on the swift short path, / praising the nature of his swift-galloping horse, / he who came marching in the night, with a bustling sound, / except for the elephant ridden by the king, / he does not seem like he will raise his shining leaf-bladed spear.","translation":"O many noble warriors! O many noble warriors of the bustling military camp, which is fenced with dense thorns resembling the thick hair of young women! Protect your king who has an army with roaring drums! Guard your male elephant with its shining, prominent tusks! However many days your battle lasts, where is the chance for others to strike? He will not even go against ordinary soldiers who have struck. Therefore, who knows what his true purpose is? Do not underestimate him thinking of your own strength! Look there! Praising the qualities of his swift-galloping horse that runs so fast it seems to measure the ground, he has marched here in the dark of night with a bustling sound. He does not seem like he will raise his shining leaf-bladed spear against anyone, except for the elephant ridden by your king!","modern":"பல சான்றோர்களே! பல சான்றோர்களே! இளம்பெண்களின் கூந்தலைப் போல நெருக்கமாக அமைக்கப்பட்ட அரிய முள்வேலியைக் கொண்ட, ஆரவாரமிக்க பாசறையில் இருக்கும் பல சான்றோர்களே! முரசு முழங்கும் படையைக் கொண்ட உங்கள் அரசனைப் பாதுகாத்துக் கொள்ளுங்கள்! ஒளிரும் நீண்ட தந்தங்களைக் கொண்ட உங்கள் ஆண் யானையையும் போற்றிப் பாதுகாத்துக் கொள்ளுங்கள்! உங்கள் போர் எத்தனை நாட்கள் நீடிக்குமோ, அத்தனை நாட்களும் உங்களில் எறிபவர்கள் எறிவது எங்கே நடக்கப் போகிறது? உங்களில் எறிந்தவர்கள் எதிரே சென்று அவர்களைத் தாக்குவதற்கும் அவன் செல்லமாட்டான். அதனால், அவன் மனதில் கருதிய நோக்கம் என்னவென்று அறிந்தவர் யார்? உங்களுடைய பலத்தைக் கொண்டு அவனை எளியவன் என்று இகழ்வதைத் தவிர்ங்கள்! அதோ பாருங்கள்! நிலத்தை அளப்பது போல வேகமாக ஓடும் தன் குதிரையின் நற்பண்புகளைப் பாராட்டி, இரவிலே ஆரவாரத்துடன் வந்து சேர்ந்திருக்கிறான். உங்கள் அரசன் ஏறி நடத்தும் யானைக்கு எதிராகவே அன்றி, வேறு எளியவர்கள் மீது தன் ஒளிரும் இலை வடிவ வேலை அவன் ஏந்தமாட்டான் போலிருக்கிறது!","explanation":"The poet Āvūr Mūlaṅkiḻār is addressing the warriors of the opposing army in their military camp, warning them about the extraordinary valor of a single warrior from his side who has arrived in the night. He advises the enemy warriors to guard their king and their chief war elephant, pointing out that this warrior is so noble and brave that he will not deign to fight ordinary soldiers or those who have already thrown their spears. He has arrived swiftly on his horse, and he will only raise his spear against the king's elephant itself. The comparison of the dense thorny fence of the camp to the thick, dark hair of young women sets a vivid visual scene of the fortified camp. The description of the horse running so fast that it seems to measure the ground highlights the speed and suddenness of his arrival. This belongs to the tumpai tiṇai (battle), specifically tāṉai maṟam (the valor of the army), showcasing the supreme confidence and selective chivalry of a hero who only targets the highest-ranking enemy.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}